# Flutter State Management

## Per-Project Choices

- **AOK**: BLoC pattern for state management
- **Atlas**: GetIt (`DI<T>()`), `ValueNotifier`, RxDart `BehaviorSubject`, feature `ViewModel` + `ValueNotifier<ScreenState>`, `UiEffect` for transient feedback, `ChangeNotifier` for lightweight app UI — full detail in synced rule `07-flutter-mobile-architecture.mdc` (applies to `apps/atlas_mobile/**/*.dart`)

## Universal Principles

- Keep state immutable (Freezed recommended for data classes)
- Single source of truth per feature
- Reactive patterns for data streams
- Proper error state handling — every async operation needs error + loading states
- Loading state for all async operations

## State Design

```dart
// Every feature state should handle:
// - Initial/idle state
// - Loading state
// - Success state with data
// - Error state with message/type
```

## Rules

- Never mutate state directly — always emit/set new state
- Dispose controllers, streams, and subscriptions in dispose()
- Avoid storing derived data in state — compute from source
- Keep state as flat as possible — avoid deeply nested state objects
- Use sealed classes or enums for state variants
